	(text "TEC power-up safe state: U108 forces the setpoint node to TEC_VZERO = 0 A.\nA unipolar DAC needs a NONZERO code for zero current, so no U101 reset state can\nmean 'TEC off' - RSTSEL=GND boots the TEC to -1.34 A of heating, and RSTSEL=VLOGIC\nwould fix that only by putting 45 mA of uncommanded current through the LASER.\nTEC_EN = PCA9538 IO3 with R121 10k to GND: the expander powers up with its IOs as\nhigh-Z inputs, so the pulldown holds TEC_EN low, ADG419 IN=0 selects S1, and the\nbridge sits at 0 A from power-on and stays there if the Teensy never boots.\nFirmware must set PCA9538 CONFIG to 0xF6 (IO0 + IO3 outputs) and raise IO3 to run."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 481.584 268.224 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "b75921fd-7062-4203-bbd2-ca5dfb3f7b6d")
	)
	(text "Decoupling bank C130-C158: one 100nF per +/-15V IC supply pin + bulk per rail - place at ICs during layout."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 606.552 358.394 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "bcd0f161-98b1-473e-8a76-6f353e1b932c")
	)
	(text "OPA551 Flag is a CURRENT SOURCE (<50 nA normal, 80/120/160 uA min/typ/max in\nthermal shutdown), NOT open-collector - so R49 is a PULL-DOWN, not a pull-up.\nnormal 2 x 50 nA x 33k = 3.3 mV (< VIL 0.99 V);  shutdown 80 uA x 33k = 2.64 V (> VIH 2.31 V).\nD23 BAT46W clamps the node to ~3.6 V so 160 uA (or both amps at once) cannot\noverdrive the PCA9538 input past its VDD+0.5 = 3.8 V abs max.\nU21 and U107 flags are wire-ORed - current-source outputs simply sum.\nFIRMWARE: HB_FAULT_LOC is now ACTIVE-HIGH (chcard_fault was active-low)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 478.536 288.544 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "c45e52f1-1ebc-4344-add6-e8d95314ebdd")
	)
